{"term":"devour","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5dc365b9467ea5752c","definition":"To eat quickly, greedily, hungrily, or ravenously.","example":"Once constituted, capital reproduces itself faster than output increases. The past devours the future.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["gobble","gorge","wolf","engorge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["all-devouring","devourable","devourer","devouringly","devouringness","devourment","interdevour","undevoured"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devour#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dfab30551237179639","definition":"To rapidly destroy, engulf, or lay waste.","example":"The fire was devouring the building.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["consume","devastate","overwhelm"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, transitive","wordFamily":["all-devouring","devourable","devourer","devouringly","devouringness","devourment","interdevour","undevoured"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devour#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ae9b2d1c2109db157","definition":"To take in avidly with the intellect or with one's gaze.","example":"She intended to devour the book.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, transitive","wordFamily":["all-devouring","devourable","devourer","devouringly","devouringness","devourment","interdevour","undevoured"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devour#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bcf07ee94208530588","definition":"To absorb or engross the mind fully, especially in a destructive manner.","example":"After the death of his wife, he wa